WEBVTT

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:25.940
Ryunosuke Akutagawa. Welcome.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.400
A cat.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.190
I'm not a cat.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.530
Call me the Acting Director.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.360
Acting Director?

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:40.400
Do you not know why you're here?

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.070
That's strange.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:47.980
When you reincarnate, you should be
given all the information you need.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.570
Can I ask you something, Acting Director?

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.230
What is it?

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:57.360
Are you sure I'm Ryunosuke Akutagawa?

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.860
So your memories are hazy?

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:32.940
Yes.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:37.570
I'm aware that I'm Ryunosuke Akutagawa.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:39.320
I could, if pressed,

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:44.400
remember the people I was close
to and the things I did in life.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:50.690
But for some reason,
it's all abstract and foggy.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.030
As for the books I've written,

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:59.230
I know of them, but have no
emotional attachment to them.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:03.940
It's very eerie, as if they aren't my own.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.570
This has never happened before,

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:09.980
but perhaps some strange error
occurred during your reincarnation.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.690
Error?

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.690
Like a broken machine.

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:19.650
Then why not try to repair yourself?

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:25.570
You authors are summoned here
to protect the books from the Taints.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:33.150
As you do this, you'll delve into
many books and meet many authors.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:39.030
Some of those authors would have
known the living Ryunosuke Akutagawa.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:43.940
So encounters... or reunitings...
will bring back my memories?

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:45.860
Yes.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:52.480
It's far more logical than simply
assuming that time will resolve it.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.320
It also seems to me like
an efficient way to get me to work.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.230
I won't deny that.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.820
Honest. I like that.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:05.900
I'll play along, Acting Director.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:10.530
For the sake of this world's literature,
and for my own sake.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:15.440
I look forward to having you as
a new Delver, Akutagawa.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:19.110
That's my first memory since I came here.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:23.690
The time when I was given a reason to fight.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.150
Episode 10

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.230
Osamu Dazai.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.980
I didn't know his name.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.400
Of course not.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.360
What did I do?

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:41.820
He came to prominence after my death.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.400
There's no time.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:50.190
Before you start asking questions... Run, Melos.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:57.820
I had never met him directly,
but chose to meet him

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:01.440
because I knew he was obsessed with me.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:06.610
I don't see myself as that interesting a person.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:11.820
But meeting someone obsessed
with Ryunosuke Akutagawa was,

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:17.690
to be honest, a potential way
to fill the hole I felt.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:23.860
When I met him, he was a very humorous person.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.980
That was, in a sense, only natural though.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:31.820
He was the kind of person who'd write
a four-meter-long letter to his teacher

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:35.820
because he wanted a prize with my name on it.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:54.190
Hey. Give us everything you've got.

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:06.320
But his obsession and the wounds in
his heart provided an opening to the Taints.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:12.320
The Taints destroy an author's
heart to change his story,

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:15.070
and then destroy his book.

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:19.980
If it was the Akutagawa Prize
that left such wounds

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:23.320
in his heart as to make him so weak...

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:28.650
It means that my coming there was correct.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:33.280
I had a duty to save his book.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:58.690
But even so... all I could do was help him.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:05.610
In the end, he had to awaken
as an author and complete his story.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:10.190
And because I couldn't do it myself...

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:14.610
Instead I was able to put
those feelings into my work!

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:16.730
That's what it means to be an author!

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:22.610
Right now, I'm Melos!

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:28.400
I'm sorry I kept you waiting, my friend.

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:40.730
When I heard his words, I thought to myself...

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.230
Thought what?

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:46.070
Strong feelings toward a story, like he has.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:48.110
Pride, you could say.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:51.360
Kan Kikuchi

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:52.530
Do I have such a thing?

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.900
But at the time,

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:58.900
I thought that the only reason
such ideas occurred to me was that

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.610
I lacked my memories.

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:09.690
If I got them back, all my feelings
towards my work would return.

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:12.900
They would have to, right?

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:17.100
Masao Kume

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:20.640
Tatsuo Hori

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.480
It was like a dream.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:27.400
Meeting the Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i>
I'd dreamed of for so long.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.730
Having him speak to me.

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.610
It's arrogance, if anything.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:39.070
We have no way of knowing
if those are really stars.

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:46.650
Yes. I think that just because something's
artificial does not diminish its sparkle.

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:53.730
Otherwise, the stories we authors
leave behind would be worthless.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:57.320
Even if we can't touch them.
Even if they aren't real.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:59.900
We can still find the stars beautiful.

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:05.690
I think that's one of the things
that makes life worth living.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:09.900
The way he thought, the words
that came out of his mouth...

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:14.940
It was just the man I'd dreamed of.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:19.980
I'll tell you the truth, I was terrified
he might sense my fear.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:22.650
I had to keep going forward.

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:28.480
It was the only way to keep
myself from falling apart.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:33.690
Oda- <i>kun</i> delved when I was inside <i>Run, Melos</i> .

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:37.480
I'm the only one who hasn't tried, right?

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:40.030
Yes, I believed...

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:44.230
...purifying books and meeting
authors who would know me

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:46.940
would eventually save me.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.650
I'm grateful to Akutagawa.

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:04.360
I was able to face up to my own
patheticness thanks to him.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:09.530
When I think about what would have happened if

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:12.360
Akutagawa and Dazai hadn't come,
I can't stop shivering.

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:15.150
So I don't want to think about it.

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:23.980
Shut up.

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:47.230
It's impossible!

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:50.190
How can Akutagawa not be Akutagawa?

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:54.980
You'll understand if you talk to him, Kikuchi!

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:55.900
I talked to him.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:58.320
The "real" him.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.230
What do you mean "the real him"?

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:04.070
Then who have we been talking to?

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:05.980
His evil twin?

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.400
There's only one possibility.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:10.400
A Taint.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:14.820
The man calling himself
Ryunosuke Akutagawa is...

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:16.440
I see.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:21.940
So he's not Ryunosuke Akutagawa
possessed by a Taint,

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:24.690
but a Taint itself.

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:25.980
Yes.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:29.070
Yes, that's the only thing that

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:33.860
would explain the presence of
two Ryunosuke Akutagawas here.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:35.980
One of them is a fake.

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:42.650
And the only thing that could create
such an identical fake would be a Taint.

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:46.530
It makes logical sense.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.030
You seem happy.

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:52.820
My hypothesis was wrong,
but it's interesting on its own.

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:55.860
We're not sure it's true, though.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.360
Yes.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:01.530
Hence why I'm talking to everyone.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:02.730
Something's wrong?

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:03.900
Yes.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:08.190
Did you feel anything wrong
as you talked to him?

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:12.650
Now that you mention it...

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:17.110
Did you feel anything wrong
as you talked to him?

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:19.530
Now that you mention it...

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:23.280
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> 's hatred of dogs was famous.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.280
So it's strange...

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:27.110
He petted one!

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:29.940
Huh? Sensei?

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:32.690
You know, I don't care, but...

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:35.360
Will you let him go?

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:39.440
I could tell because we were enemies...

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:44.030
Ryu- <i>kun</i> was a little different
than everyone else.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:48.320
I don't know why, but... he was
the only one who didn't totally agree

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:51.110
to our plan to catch the Taint.

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:53.820
I remember there was this
strange sense of resistance.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:58.980
What's that clam?

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:01.820
It moved.

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:07.190
Yes, I am the clam that killed Osamu Dazai!

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:08.150
What?

00:13:08.150 --> 00:13:10.690
You got killed by a clam?

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:12.570
Who would do something so terrible?

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:17.320
Right? They sent me to hell,
which means they've got good taste.

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:19.070
Is he happy?

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:21.480
Ango can be like that sometimes.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.900
Do you remember who killed you?

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:26.440
He probably got stabbed in a fight.

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:30.730
If it was a fight, I wouldn't lose.
I'm not like you.

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:32.780
You're picking a fight with me
when you're a corpse?

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:34.360
Fine.

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:35.480
A chair?

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:36.980
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:51.780
He was always the fastest
to escape from the illusions.

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:54.780
So you finally awakened?

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:58.940
Unbelievable. I'm the first to awaken?

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.530
Look around.

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:06.570
If he was a different sort of creature than us,

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:09.320
it would explain what happened then.

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:10.320
But...

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:15.230
Ryu- <i>kun</i> was serious, then.

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:20.030
He was seriously trying to save me and my book.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:26.530
I can't see a fake doing that.

00:14:27.690 --> 00:14:29.280
Now what?

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:31.980
Sorry, but I don't think I can hold back!

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:38.610
I want my books to disappear!

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:47.360
I see.

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:50.280
Making the will of an author his ally

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:54.820
gave the Taint the power to
interfere with the story directly.

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:58.400
This just doesn't make sense!

00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:04.280
I've delved with him many times!
Fought with him many times!

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:07.280
So I can tell you for sure that
he was more serious about

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:12.320
protecting the books than anybody else.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:16.230
The early Akutagawa,
who entranced readers with his stories,

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:14.220
No Longer Human

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:19.650
and the later Akutagawa,
who rejected that style,

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:22.360
were different people.

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:24.440
An interesting theory.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:29.690
So does that mean there
are two Ryunosuke Akutagawas?

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:33.860
It's hard to imagine a different
person impersonating you.

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:39.070
So I came up with a different idea.

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:47.650
Perhaps the later works were written
by a Taint within Ryunosuke Akutagawa.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:51.190
So they'd possess me, take over my body,

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:55.440
and force me to write new works
that denied my earlier ones?

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:57.360
Is that your theory?

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:59.820
Don't you find it fascinating?

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:00.820
No.

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:05.570
What would that make you, if that were true?

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:10.480
Would half of you be a Taint?

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:17.980
All this and more in Toson Shimazaki's
shocking new novel.

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:22.480
It would make for a fun plot.

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:23.690
I see.

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:25.820
I hadn't thought of that.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:31.980
Begone from my sight.

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:36.940
Release me, please.

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:38.730
I can't.

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:41.820
I have to go.

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:48.900
Are you Ryunosuke Akutagawa? Or...

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:53.400
I just want to save Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:05.940
What are you doing?

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:08.320
I'm interested in you now.

00:17:15.190 --> 00:17:17.320
I hope it works.

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:18.730
Pray for me.

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:34.980
He tried his best to save me!

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:39.530
Are you betraying me?

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:45.360
Damn it!

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:47.190
Why?

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:49.900
Ango!

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:57.360
Why does everyone look so happy all the time?

00:17:58.360 --> 00:17:59.860
Tell me. Why?

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.820
And still you laugh with each other.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:15.360
Then...

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:16.650
Think!

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:20.570
Keep thinking!

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:26.860
Dazai- <i>kun</i> .

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:33.070
I can't have you dying of drink.

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:42.190
I'll still struggle my hardest to be normal.

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:47.030
That's ridiculous.

00:18:47.030 --> 00:18:51.480
I'd never trust my life
to somebody I couldn't count on.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:54.440
We risked our lives to fight with each other.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:57.570
I believe in Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> .

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.530
He's Akutagawa.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.530
It's the only conclusion.

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:04.360
Hell if I know.

00:19:04.360 --> 00:19:05.860
He's one of us.

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:10.980
I refuse to believe he's a fake or a Taint.

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:15.070
He did everything he could to give me this.

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:18.070
Could a Taint do that?

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:19.900
He's Akutagawa!

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:24.440
If you keep talking crap about him
being a fake, you'll regret it!

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:27.480
I think it's Ryu- <i>kun</i> too.

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:31.650
You guys came out of nowhere,
what the hell do you know?

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:34.360
He's Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:35.400
He has to be.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:36.610
It's the opposite.

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:39.150
We can tell because we just got here.

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:41.650
Where do you think we've been?

00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:42.980
Where?

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:45.480
The World Rift?

00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:46.980
Rift?

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:49.480
The Alchemist detected something wrong

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:53.860
and tried to reincarnate me
and the authors close to me.

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:55.900
But failed.

00:19:55.900 --> 00:20:01.650
An external force blocked certain
authors from being summoned.

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:06.690
And you're saying that was the other Akutagawa?

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:13.030
A Taint inside this building could
affect reincarnations, correct?

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:17.780
Either way, we were called
but couldn't come out.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:20.480
And were trapped in the rift.

00:20:22.190 --> 00:20:23.320
What?

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:30.280
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> ?

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:38.030
But for some reason,
the blocking suddenly stopped.

00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:41.980
And so we were able to reincarnate here.

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:43.860
Why?

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:48.900
The obvious assumption is that something
happened to the one doing the blocking.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:52.030
Sudden exhaustion, for instance.

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:54.110
Get away from him!

00:20:55.650 --> 00:21:00.820
Anyway, we should decide what to do immediately.

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:02.150
What to do?

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:03.610
Do you mean?

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:05.530
He's a Taint.

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.030
There's only one thing to do.

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:08.400
Hell no!

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:11.480
Weren't you listening to us?

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:14.320
He's been with us this whole time!

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:15.650
He's one of us!

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:17.650
I'm sorry.

00:21:17.650 --> 00:21:21.070
This must be all my fault.

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:23.360
What do you mean?

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:27.610
I need to tell you about him.

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:31.780
And why I created him.

00:21:52.940 --> 00:21:56.940
In a Bamboo Grove

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.970
"Literary Gourmet."

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:30.970
A Man's Pride and Curry Rice

00:23:31.570 --> 00:23:32.570
Yum!

00:23:32.570 --> 00:23:38.190
"Curry Rice - Slowly stewed curry
with sweet vegetables and spices."

00:23:32.570 --> 00:23:35.400
Why is curry rice so good?

00:23:35.400 --> 00:23:38.190
The red ginger with it is good, too.

00:23:38.190 --> 00:23:41.530
I had bean curry for
the first time the other day.

00:23:41.530 --> 00:23:44.820
It was amazing...

00:23:41.530 --> 00:23:44.820
Curry continues to entrance mankind.

00:23:44.820 --> 00:23:47.110
The red ginger is just there
to make it look better.

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:49.860
Like me and him...

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:52.440
But the minor roles are trying their best too!

00:23:52.440 --> 00:23:56.110
Sliced apart, covered in spice,
and put to the flame...

00:23:56.110 --> 00:23:58.980
Red ginger has its pride too!

00:23:58.980 --> 00:24:00.690
What are you talking about?
